    <!-- ===== Azure Client ID 获取引导（v0.1.3） ===== -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Title">How to get an Azure Client ID</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Sub">Microsoft paid login requires a free Azure Client ID ("app code") — this is Microsoft policy: every app registers its own ID. It takes about 3 minutes and only once.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Step1">Open the Azure portal (button below) and sign in with your Microsoft account (free, no card needed).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Step2">Search "App registrations" in the top search bar, then click "New registration".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Step3">Any name (e.g. HardmacroCraft); under "Supported account types" choose option 3: Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts; leave redirect URI empty.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Step4">Click "Register"; on the Overview page copy the "Application (client) ID" — that is your Azure Client ID.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Step5">Crucial: in your app go to "Authentication" → scroll to the bottom "Advanced settings" → set "Allow public client flows" to "Enable" → Save. Device-code login fails without this.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Step6">Paste the ID into Launcher → Settings → Azure Client ID, save, then use Microsoft login on the home page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.HaveId">Got the ID? Paste it into Settings → Azure Client ID → Save, then click "Microsoft Login" on the home page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.OpenPortal">Open Azure Portal</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.OpenRegister">Open "App registrations"</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.Close">Got it</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Azure.OpenGuide">How to get an Azure Client ID? (step-by-step)</sys:String>

